IO-56: clear a conduit's normal-flow and inlet-control flags when it is dry

dwflow_findConduitFlow() resets Link.normalFlow and Link.inletControl only
after its early return for a dry or closed conduit, so a conduit that was
normal-flow limited (or inlet controlled) on its last flowing step keeps
the flag for as long as it stays dry, and stats_updateLinkStats() adds
every one of those steps to the Norm Ltd (Inlet Ctrl) time of the Flow
Classification Summary. Clear both flags on the early-return path too. The
flags are read only by the statistics, so the hydraulics do not change.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-56_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/dwflow.c b/src/legacy/engine/dwflow.c
index 828431b..296f31a 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/dwflow.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/dwflow.c
@@ -200,6 +200,8 @@ void  dwflow_findConduitFlow(int linkIndex, int steps, double omega, double dt)
         Link[linkIndex].newDepth = MIN(yMid, Link[linkIndex].xsect.yFull);
         Link[linkIndex].newVolume = Conduit[k].a1 * link_getLength(linkIndex) * barrels;
         Link[linkIndex].newFlow = 0.0;
+        Link[linkIndex].inletControl = FALSE;
+        Link[linkIndex].normalFlow = FALSE;
         return;
     }
 
